# The Saving and loading tutorial (docs/tutorials/saving.md, #295): its
# steps, in a copy of the finished project (docs/tutorials/saving/), and its
# screenshots (scripts/docs/screenshots.sh tutorial_saving copies them to
# docs/images/tutorial-saving_*.png). The drive makes scripts/game.lua a
# global script again, saves a game from Simulate into the drive's own
# user-data folder, plays it (Play continues it), and runs the project's
# save tests in the Tests tab.
# drive: project docs/tutorials/saving
wait 5
key escape

# 1. The global script: taken away, then made global as the page says.
rclick @asset:scripts/game.lua
click @ctx:remove-global
wait 2
expect item:asset.global:scripts/game.lua == missing
rclick @asset:scripts/game.lua
click @ctx:make-global
wait 2
expect item:asset.global:scripts/game.lua == visible
expect file:project.json contains {"name": "Game", "script": "scripts/game.lua"}
click @toolbar.settings
click @settings.page:Globals
expect item:settings.global-name:0 == visible
expect item:settings.global-problem:0 == missing
annotate @settings.global-name:0 The global's name: every script reaches the table as Game
annotate @settings.global-script:0 The script it is loaded from, once, before any scene
screenshot tutorial-saving_global
click @settings.cancel
wait 2

# 2. The title screen in Simulate: an empty slot, then a game saved from
# the Lua line (Game:new_game writes slot_1.json in the user-data folder).
dblclick @asset:scenes/title.scene.json
wait 10
expect scene contains title.scene.json
click @hier:Menu
key shift+home
wait 3
click @menu:Game
click @menu:Game/Simulate in Editor
wait 20
expect node:Summary.prop.text == Slot 1: empty
expect node:Continue.enabled == false
click @bottom:console
click @console.lua
type Game:new_game(1); Game.data.gems = 40; Save.flush(); Scene.find_node("Menu"):get_script():show(1)
key enter
wait 5
expect node:Summary.prop.text == Slot 1: 40 gems, pick level 1
expect node:Continue.enabled == true
expect abs-file:$PROJECT/../userdata/slot_1.json contains "gems": 40
expect abs-file:$PROJECT/../userdata/settings.json contains "last_slot": 1
annotate @node:Summary The summary: read from slot_1.json
annotate @node:Continue Continue and Delete show when the slot has a game
annotate @node:Slot Picks slot 1, 2 or 3
screenshot tutorial-saving_title
click @menu:Game
click @menu:Game/Simulate in Editor
wait 5

# 3. The settings screen: a UI Slider and a UI Checkbox.
dblclick @asset:scenes/settings.scene.json
wait 10
expect scene contains settings.scene.json
click @hier:Menu/Volume
key shift+home
wait 5
expect node:Volume.prop.maxValue == 1
annotate @node:Volume A UI Slider, 0 to 1: value_changed sets the volume
annotate @node:Fullscreen A UI Checkbox: value_changed switches fullscreen
annotate @node:Back Back writes settings.json
screenshot tutorial-saving_settings

# 4. Played (without the drives' Show Colliders): Play uses the same
# user-data folder, so the game continues the slot saved above.
dblclick @asset:scenes/main.scene.json
wait 10
click @menu:Game
click @menu:Game/Show Colliders in Game
expect log contains Colliders hidden in the game
game-args --frames 60 --screenshot $SHOTS/05_tutorial-saving_game.png --dump-scene $SHOTS/game_scene.json
key f6
wait-until game == stopped timeout=900
expect abs-file:$SHOTS/game_scene.json contains "Gems: 40"

# 5. The project's save tests (tests/saves_test.lua) in the Tests tab.
click @bottom:tests
wait 3
drag 640,592 640,330
wait 3
expect item:tests.row:test_mined_gems_are_saved == visible
click @tests.run-all
wait-until log contains Tests: 3 passed, 0 failed timeout=1800
wait 3
annotate @tests.row:test_version_1_save_is_migrated A test writes a version 1 save and checks the migration
screenshot tutorial-saving_tests
